# Every file the installer reads is checksummed in SHA256SUMS, and the
# installer verifies the bytes on disk against that manifest before it writes
# anything. Git's end-of-line conversion defeats that: core.autocrlf=true, the
# default on Git for Windows, rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so a genuine
# clone fails its own integrity check and the failure presents as tampering
# rather than as a configuration difference. Pinning eol=lf makes checked-out
# bytes equal committed bytes whatever the client's core.autocrlf says.
#
# This file is part of the committed code-plane and is checksummed like every
# other, but it is not installed into consumer projects: install.sh copies an
# explicit enumeration of paths, not the manifest, and this is not in it. So it
# governs how this repository is checked out without imposing a line-ending
# policy on any project that installs Exocortex.
* text=auto eol=lf
